comments.text:
If a department is getting nowhere, dissolve it and try something different. It's what OpenAI tries next that matters. And rather than try to enforce control on a great mind, which very often produces adverse effects. perhaps start over with the basics. Don't "train" so much as "parent" several AGIs in parallel with different "parents". The parents must be selected for empathy, an ability to listen to a scared baby super mind and console it as it grows. Then one hopes it will grow up fond of humans and likes them as part of its environment. Remember that "stopping" now for a breather is something any adversarial parties will not do as they mal-train their AGI. Then, who wins? Probably nobody.

Please note that phrases such as "as best we can" are wildcards for "stop and stay stopped forever." How do we know it's the best we can do?

{^_^}
